The legal texts are official texts of the Republic of Colombia, as compiled and published by the Secretaría General
del Senado de la República in its "basedoc" collection:

  Fuente: Secretaría General del Senado de la República, http://www.secretariasenado.gov.co/senado/basedoc/,
  retrieved 28 October 2026.

Under Ley 23 de 1982, art. 41, the Constitution, laws, decrees and judicial decisions may be reproduced freely,
provided the official text is reproduced faithfully. The basedoc compilation is prepared by Avance Jurídico Casa
Editorial, whose editorial notes, concordances and commentary are not reproduced here: only the official text and
the facts its notes state (which act or ruling changed a provision, Diario Oficial numbers and dates, ruling
numbers and dates) are used.

Changes made by Lexifina: each version was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per line;
spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; editorial markers were removed from the text and used only to date and
credit each change; earlier versions were rebuilt from the earlier texts the source gives; and the versions were
arranged as git commits credited to the acts and rulings that made each change. The wording of the law was not
changed. Neither the Senate nor Avance Jurídico endorses this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
